{"id":"leetcode-63","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"Unique Paths II","summary":"Given an m x n grid where certain squares are marked as obstacles (represented by 1) and others as open spaces (represented by 0), calculate the number of unique paths from the top-left corner to the bottom-right corner.","statement":"Given an m x n grid where certain squares are marked as obstacles (represented by 1) and others as open spaces (represented by 0), calculate the number of unique paths from the top-left corner to the bottom-right corner. The robot can only move either down or right at any point in time, and it cannot pass through any obstacles. Return the total number of unique paths that avoid obstacles and lead to the bottom-right corner. The test cases are structured such that the solution will not exceed 2 * 10^9.","constraints":["A rectangular 1–100 by 1–100 grid contains only 0 (open) or 1 (blocked).","Move only right/down, never through blocked cells. The answer is at most 2×10^9."],"topics":["matrices","recursion","dynamic-programming"],"prerequisites":[],"signature":{"name":"obstacle_paths","parameters":[{"name":"obstacle_grid","annotation":"list[list[int]]","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"int","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"values","result_mode":"return","mutated_parameter":null,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"def obstacle_paths(obstacle_grid: list[list[int]]) -> int:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def obstacle_paths(obstacle_grid):\n    rows, cols = len(obstacle_grid), len(obstacle_grid[0])\n    memo = {}\n    def visit(row, col):\n        if row >= rows or col >= cols or obstacle_grid[row][col] == 1:\n            return 0\n        if row == rows - 1 and col == cols - 1:\n            return 1\n        if (row, col) not in memo:\n            memo[row, col] = visit(row + 1, col) + visit(row, col + 1)\n        return memo[row, col]\n    return visit(0, 0)\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def obstacle_paths(obstacle_grid):\n    rows, cols = len(obstacle_grid), len(obstacle_grid[0])\n    memo = {}\n    def visit(row, col):\n        if row >= rows or col >= cols:\n            return 0\n        if row == rows - 1 and col == cols - 1:\n            return 1\n        if (row, col) not in memo:\n            memo[row, col] = visit(row + 1, col) + visit(row, col + 1)\n        return memo[row, col]\n    return visit(0, 0)\n","def obstacle_paths(obstacle_grid):\n    rows, cols = len(obstacle_grid), len(obstacle_grid[0])\n    memo = {}\n    def visit(row, col):\n        if row >= rows or col >= cols or obstacle_grid[row][col] == 1:\n            return 0\n        if row == rows - 1 and col == cols - 1:\n            return 0\n        if (row, col) not in memo:\n            memo[row, col] = visit(row + 1, col) + visit(row, col + 1)\n        return memo[row, col]\n    return visit(0, 0)\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(mn)","target_space_complexity":"O(mn) memo plus O(m+n) stack","estimated_minutes":35,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":2,"prerequisites":1,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":1,"edge_cases":0},"hints":["An invalid or blocked cell contributes no routes; an open destination contributes one.","Recursively add the answers from the right and down neighbors, caching by coordinates.","Check bounds and obstacles first, then the destination. Memoize visit(r+1,c)+visit(r,c+1).","Without caching, different paths repeatedly solve the same remaining subgrid."],"editorial":"Define visit(r,c) as the number of valid routes from that cell to the destination. Outside or blocked cells return zero; the open destination returns one. Every other result is the sum from its two allowed next cells. Memoization ensures each coordinate is solved at most once. The recursion has depth at most m+n; a bottom-up row-array solution can reduce memory to O(n). The oracle independently enumerates complete move sequences and checks every visited cell.","tests":[{"id":"lc-63-1","arguments":[[[0,0,0],[0,1,0],[0,0,0]]],"expected":2,"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"The center is blocked. Only the route along the top/right edges and the route along the left/bottom edges remain.","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-63-2","arguments":[[[0,1],[0,0]]],"expected":1,"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"Right is blocked at the start, so the only route goes down then right.","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-63-3","arguments":[[[0]]],"expected":1,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-63-4","arguments":[[[1]]],"expected":0,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-63-5","arguments":[[[0,0]]],"expected":1,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-63-6","arguments":[[[0,1]]],"expected":0,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-63-7","arguments":[[[1,0]]],"expected":0,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-63-8","arguments":[[[0],[0]]],"expected":1,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-63-9","arguments":[[[0],[1]]],"expected":0,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-63-10","arguments":[[[1],[0]]],"expected":0,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-63-11","arguments":[[[0,0],[0,0]]],"expected":2,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-63-12","arguments":[[[0,0],[0,1]]],"expected":0,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-63-13","arguments":[[[1,0],[0,0]]],"expected":0,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-63-